/* Lessons.swift */
"看懂一张照片" = "Reading a Photo";
"调整明暗" = "Light and Dark";
"颜色" = "Color";
"拍摄的原理" = "How Cameras Work";
"视频与 Live" = "Video and Live";
"直方图从哪里来" = "Where the Histogram Comes From";
"调色软件里那座「小山」到底是什么？" = "What is that little “mountain” in every photo editor?";
"照片由小格子组成" = "A photo is made of tiny squares";
"放大到足够大，任何照片都是一格一格的像素。每一格只有一种颜色。" = "Zoom in far enough and every photo is a grid of pixels. Each square has just one color.";
"先只看明暗" = "Look only at brightness";
"把颜色去掉，每一格只剩下一个亮度：0 是纯黑，100 是纯白。" = "Take the color away and each square is left with a single brightness: 0 is pure black, 100 is pure white.";
"亮度变成高度" = "Brightness becomes height";
"把每一格的亮度当成高度：越亮的格子越高，越暗的越矮。照片就变成一片立体的柱子。拖动画面转一转，从侧面看看。" = "Use each square's brightness as its height: the brighter the square, the taller it is; the darker, the shorter. The photo becomes a field of 3D columns. Drag the view to turn it and look from the side.";
"按亮度排队" = "Line them up by brightness";
"把所有格子按亮度从左到右排好，一样亮的叠在同一列。叠出来的形状，就是直方图。" = "Line up all the squares from dark on the left to bright on the right, stacking equally bright ones in the same column. The shape of the stacks is the histogram.";
"读一读你的照片" = "Read your own photo";
"山峰在哪里，照片的大部分就在哪里。左边高说明暗的多，右边高说明亮的多。" = "Wherever the peak is, that's where most of the photo is. High on the left means lots of dark; high on the right, lots of bright.";
"这张照片的大部分在哪个区域？" = "Which zone is most of this photo in?";
"看直方图最高、最宽的那一段落在哪个区域。" = "Look at which zone the tallest, widest part of the histogram falls in.";
"五个亮度区" = "The Five Brightness Zones";
"「提亮暗部」里的暗部，到底是哪一部分？" = "When people say “lift the shadows”, which part do they mean?";
"把亮度分成五段" = "Split brightness into five";
"从左到右：最暗部、暗部、中间调、亮部、最亮部。点一个区域，照片上只保留属于它的地方。" = "From left to right: darkest, shadows, midtones, highlights, brightest. Click a zone and the photo shows only the parts that belong to it.";
"亮和暗都可以是对的" = "Bright or dark can both be right";
"白墙、雪景常常大部分在亮部，夜景大部分在暗部。直方图偏向一边不等于拍错了，要看你想要的感觉。" = "White walls and snow scenes are mostly in the highlights; night scenes mostly in the shadows. A histogram leaning to one side doesn't mean the shot is wrong; it depends on the feeling you want.";
"一张雪景的直方图大部分在右边，说明什么？" = "A snow scene's histogram is mostly on the right. What does that tell you?";
"一定过曝了" = "It must be overexposed";
"画面以亮的东西为主，可能正好合适" = "The scene is mostly bright things; it may be just right";
"相机坏了" = "The camera is broken";
"直方图只说明亮度怎么分布。只有贴着最右边、出现纯白时，才是真的丢了细节。" = "The histogram only shows how brightness is spread. Detail is really lost only when it's pressed against the far right and turns pure white.";
"纯白和死黑" = "Pure White and Pure Black";
"为什么有些天空怎么调都是一片白？" = "Why do some skies stay white no matter what you do?";
"亮到头，就没有细节了" = "Past the limit, the detail is gone";
"拖动曝光。太亮的地方会变成纯白（标红），太暗的地方变成纯黑（标蓝）。直方图会在边上堆成一堵墙。" = "Drag Exposure. Areas that get too bright turn pure white (marked red) and areas too dark turn pure black (marked blue). The histogram piles up into a wall at the edge.";
"拍摄时天空已经是纯白，后期把高光往下拉会怎样？" = "The sky was already pure white when you shot it. What happens if you pull Highlights down afterwards?";
"会变成蓝色" = "It turns blue";
"只会变成一片灰，细节找不回来" = "It just turns flat gray; the detail can't come back";
"能找回云的细节" = "The cloud detail comes back";
"纯白意味着相机没有记录到那里的差别。拍的时候就要留住：降低一点曝光，或者打开 HDR。" = "Pure white means the camera recorded no differences there. You have to keep them when shooting: lower the exposure a little or turn on HDR.";
"曝光和亮度不一样" = "Exposure Isn't Brightness";
"都是变亮，为什么有时候天空先「爆」掉？" = "Both make things brighter, so why does the sky sometimes blow out first?";
"一个乘，一个加" = "One multiplies, one adds";
"曝光像多进一倍的光：越亮的地方增加得越多。亮度更像整体往上挪一点。拖两个滑块，看右边的线怎么变。" = "Exposure is like letting in twice the light: brighter areas gain the most. Brightness is more like moving everything up a little. Drag both sliders and watch how the line on the right changes.";
"照片的天空已经很亮、地面偏暗，想提亮地面，先用哪个？" = "The sky is already very bright and the ground is dark. To brighten the ground, which do you try first?";
"亮度或阴影" = "Brightness or Shadows";
"曝光会让本来就亮的天空先溢出；亮度和阴影对亮部影响更小。" = "Exposure makes the already-bright sky clip first; Brightness and Shadows affect the highlights less.";
"四个滑块各管一段" = "Four Sliders, Four Ranges";
"高光、阴影、白色、黑色有什么区别？" = "What's the difference between Highlights, Shadows, Whites and Blacks?";
"每个滑块只动自己的那段" = "Each slider moves only its own range";
"选一个滑块拖动。照片上亮起来的是它改变的地方，直方图上阴影部分是它作用的亮度范围。" = "Pick a slider and drag it. What lights up in the photo is what it changes, and the shaded part of the histogram is the brightness range it acts on.";
"逆光人像，脸太暗但背景的天空正好，应该动哪个？" = "In a backlit portrait the face is too dark but the sky behind is just right. Which slider do you move?";
"脸在暗部，阴影只提亮暗部，天空几乎不受影响。" = "The face is in the shadows. Shadows brightens only the dark areas, so the sky is barely touched.";
"曲线：把旧亮度换成新亮度" = "Curves: Old Brightness In, New Brightness Out";
"曲线看起来很专业，其实只回答一个问题。" = "Curves look technical, but they answer just one question.";
"横轴是原来，竖轴是现在" = "Across is before, up is after";
"曲线竖在左边：横着是原来的亮度，竖着是现在的亮度，斜线上的每一点都在说「原来多亮，现在还是多亮」。右边是你照片的亮度地形，柱子的高度就是现在的亮度。拖动中间的点，看哪一段的柱子变了。" = "The curve stands on the left: across is the old brightness, up is the new brightness, and every point on the diagonal says “as bright as before, still as bright”. On the right is your photo's brightness terrain, where each column's height is its brightness now. Drag the middle point and see which columns change.";
"三种常见形状" = "Three common shapes";
"整体往上 = 变亮，柱子整体升高；往下 = 变暗。S 形 = 暗的更暗、亮的更亮：矮的柱子更矮，高的更高，地形更陡，对比更强。点按钮切换，看地形、照片和直方图。" = "Moved up = brighter, so the columns all rise; down = darker. S-shaped = darker darks and brighter brights: short columns get shorter, tall ones get taller, the terrain gets steeper and contrast goes up. Click the buttons and watch the terrain, the photo and the histogram.";
"照片发灰、没有层次，最常用哪种曲线？" = "The photo looks gray and flat. Which curve is most commonly used?";
"S 形" = "S-shaped";
"整体往上" = "Moved up";
"整体往下" = "Moved down";
"S 形把直方图向两边拉开，画面就不再发灰。" = "An S curve stretches the histogram toward both ends, so the image no longer looks gray.";
"白平衡与色温" = "White Balance and Color Temperature";
"为什么在室内拍的照片总是发黄？" = "Why do photos taken indoors always look yellow?";
"光本身有颜色" = "Light has a color";
"烛光和灯泡偏橙，正午阳光接近白，阴天和树荫偏蓝。用开尔文（K）表示：数字越小越暖，越大越冷。选一种光，看同一张照片被染成什么样；右边的立方体里，整团颜色会偏离中间的灰色竖线。" = "Candles and light bulbs are orange, midday sun is close to white, and overcast skies and shade are blue. It's measured in kelvin (K): lower is warmer, higher is cooler. Pick a light and see how it tints the same photo; in the cube on the right, the whole cloud of colors moves away from the gray line in the middle.";
"找一个本该是白或灰的地方" = "Find something that should be white or gray";
"白纸、白墙、灰色路面在真实世界里没有颜色。点照片里这样的地方，光集会把它校正成中性灰：你点的颜色回到灰色竖线上，整张照片的偏色就跟着消失。" = "White paper, white walls and gray pavement have no color in real life. Click a spot like that in the photo and Lucet makes it neutral gray: the color you picked returns to the gray line, and the cast disappears from the whole photo.";
"暖黄灯光下拍的照片发黄，色温滑块该往哪边？" = "A photo shot under warm yellow light looks yellow. Which way should the Temperature slider go?";
"往冷（左）" = "Cooler (left)";
"往暖（右）" = "Warmer (right)";
"照片偏暖，就往冷的方向补回来。日落等想保留的暖色，可以只补一部分。" = "If the photo is too warm, move toward cool to balance it. For warmth you want to keep, like a sunset, correct only part of it.";
"HSL：只改一种颜色" = "HSL: Change Just One Color";
"怎样只让天空更蓝，而草地不变？" = "How do you make only the sky bluer and leave the grass alone?";
"一个颜色，三个数" = "One color, three numbers";
"任何颜色都能用三个数找到：绕圈是色相（哪种颜色，红→黄→绿→青→蓝→紫），向外是饱和度（多鲜艳），向上是明亮度（多亮）。色轮就是这根圆柱的俯视图。拖动色轮上的点和下面的滑块。" = "Any color can be found with three numbers: going around is hue (which color: red → yellow → green → aqua → blue → purple), going outward is saturation (how vivid), going up is luminance (how bright). The color wheel is this cylinder seen from above. Drag the dot on the wheel and the slider below.";
"只挑出一种颜色" = "Pick out one color";
"选一个色系，照片上只有这种颜色保持彩色。再拖它的色相、饱和度、明亮度：圆柱里这个色系的点会跟着移动，其他颜色不会动。" = "Choose a color range and only that color stays in color in the photo. Drag its hue, saturation and luminance: the dots of that range move in the cylinder, and the other colors stay put.";
"想让天空更深一点、草地不受影响，应该调什么？" = "You want the sky a little deeper without affecting the grass. What should you adjust?";
"整体饱和度" = "Overall saturation";
"曝光往下" = "Lower the exposure";
"蓝色的明亮度往下" = "Lower the blue luminance";
"HSL 只作用在选中的颜色上：压暗蓝色，天空变深，绿色的草地不变。" = "HSL acts only on the chosen color: darken the blues and the sky deepens while the green grass stays the same.";
"光圈：数字越大，开口越小" = "Aperture: Bigger Number, Smaller Opening";
"为什么 ƒ/4 比 ƒ/2.8 的光圈小？" = "Why is ƒ/4 a smaller aperture than ƒ/2.8?";
"ƒ 后面是一个除数" = "The number after ƒ divides";
"光圈开口的直径 = 焦距 ÷ ƒ 值。所以 ƒ 值越大，开口越小，进来的光越少。ƒ 值每乘以 1.4，进光量减半。拖动滑块，再转着看：光圈挡住外圈的光，只有开口里的光能到达传感器。" = "The opening's diameter = focal length ÷ the ƒ-number. So the bigger the ƒ-number, the smaller the opening and the less light gets in. Each time the ƒ-number is multiplied by 1.4, the light is halved. Drag the slider, then turn the view: the aperture blocks the outer light and only the light through the opening reaches the sensor.";
"开口还决定背景有多虚" = "The opening also decides how blurry the background is";
"开口大（ƒ 值小），空间里只有很薄的一层（半透明的板）是清楚的，前后的东西就虚；开口小，这一层变厚，前后都清楚。拖动看看，旁边是拍出来的样子。" = "With a wide opening (small ƒ-number) only a thin layer of space (the translucent slab) is sharp, and whatever is in front of or behind it blurs; with a small opening the layer gets thicker and front and back are both sharp. Drag to see; the photo it makes is next to it.";
"想拍背景虚化的人像，应该怎么选？" = "For a portrait with a blurry background, what do you choose?";
"ƒ 值小 = 开口大 = 清楚的范围薄，背景更虚。" = "Small ƒ-number = wide opening = a thin sharp zone and a blurrier background.";
"快门、ISO 和曝光三角" = "Shutter, ISO and the Exposure Triangle";
"同样亮的照片，为什么有的糊、有的满是噪点？" = "Two photos are equally bright. Why is one blurry and the other full of noise?";
"快门：开多久" = "Shutter: how long it's open";
"把时间想成纵深：越远越晚。一个球横穿画面，它的路线是一条斜线。快门开着的那段时间是一块玻璃板：板越厚，进来的光越多，球在板里走过的路也越长，落到照片上就是拖影。拖动快门，再转一转看看。手持拍摄，快门最好快于 1/焦距 秒。" = "Think of time as depth: the farther away, the later. A ball crosses the frame, and its path through space and time is a slanted line. The time the shutter stays open is a pane of glass: the thicker the pane, the more light gets in and the farther the ball travels inside it, which lands on the photo as a trail. Drag the shutter, then turn the view. Handheld, keep the shutter faster than 1/focal length seconds.";
"ISO：把信号放大" = "ISO: amplifying the signal";
"传感器是一格一格的小格子，光一颗一颗落进去，每一格数一数收到多少。光不够时，ISO 把每一格的数字统统放大，照片就变亮。可光子是随机落下来的，相邻的格子数目总有差别，放大以后，这些差别就成了噪点。拖动 ISO，看柱子怎么变。" = "The sensor is a grid of tiny cells. Light lands in them one photon at a time, and each cell counts what it caught. When there isn't enough light, ISO multiplies every cell's count and the photo gets brighter. But photons land at random, so neighboring cells never catch quite the same number, and multiplying turns those differences into noise. Drag ISO and watch the columns.";
"三个旋钮，同一个亮度" = "Three dials, one brightness";
"光圈、快门、ISO 是空间里的三条轴，每条轴都指向「更多光」，也各有代价：景深、拖影、噪点。那块斜板上的每个点，亮度都正好；点离开板，就是亮了或暗了几档。下面几种拍法都在板上，只是落在不同的位置。" = "Aperture, shutter and ISO are three axes in space. Each points toward “more light” and each has a cost: depth of field, motion blur, noise. Every point on the tilted slab has just the right brightness; a point off the slab is some stops too bright or too dark. The recipes below all lie on the slab, just in different places.";
"夜里拍街景，照片太暗又不想糊，先试哪个？" = "Shooting a street at night, the photo is too dark and you don't want blur. What do you try first?";
"开大光圈，再适当提高 ISO" = "Open the aperture, then raise ISO a little";
"把 ISO 调到最低" = "Set ISO as low as it goes";
"把快门调慢很多" = "Make the shutter much slower";
"先用光圈多进光；还不够再提 ISO。快门太慢，手一抖就糊了。" = "Let in more light with the aperture first, and raise ISO if that's not enough. With a very slow shutter, the slightest shake blurs the photo.";
"焦距：广角和长焦" = "Focal Length: Wide and Telephoto";
"同一个位置，为什么手机「2 倍」「5 倍」拍出的画面差这么多？" = "From the same spot, why do a phone's “2×” and “5×” give such different pictures?";
"焦距决定看多宽" = "Focal length decides how wide you see";
"焦距越短，看到的范围越宽（广角）；越长，越像望远镜（长焦）。拖动焦距：立体图里相机看到的是一个楔形，焦距越长楔形越窄，照片只装得下中间那一小块。手机上的「2 倍」「5 倍」，就是在换焦距。" = "The shorter the focal length, the wider the view (wide-angle); the longer, the more like a telescope (telephoto). Drag the focal length: in the 3D view the camera sees a wedge, and the longer the lens, the narrower the wedge, so the photo only holds a small piece from the middle. A phone's “2×” and “5×” are changing focal length.";
"长焦会把背景「拉近」" = "Telephoto “pulls” the background closer";
"让人在画面里一样大，长焦需要站得更远（上面的图是从上往下看）。楔形变窄，同一座山占的画面比例就变大，背景显得又大又近；广角则背景很远、很小。这叫透视压缩。" = "To keep a person the same size in the frame, a telephoto lens needs you to stand farther away (the picture above is seen from above). The wedge gets narrower, so the same mountain takes up a larger share of the frame and the background looks big and close; with wide-angle, the background looks far away and small. This is called perspective compression.";
"在小房间里拍一大群人的合影，选哪种焦距？" = "For a big group photo in a small room, which focal length do you pick?";
"广角（短焦距）" = "Wide-angle (short focal length)";
"长焦（长焦距）" = "Telephoto (long focal length)";
"广角能在近距离装下更宽的画面；长焦要退得很远，小房间里做不到。" = "Wide-angle fits a wider view from close up; telephoto needs you to back far away, which a small room doesn't allow.";
"帧率与快门" = "Frame Rate and Shutter";
"为什么视频的快门不能像拍照那样越快越好？" = "Why isn't a faster shutter always better for video, the way it can be for photos?";
"视频是一秒很多张照片" = "Video is many photos per second";
"24 帧就是每秒 24 张，60 帧是 60 张。帧越多，动作越顺滑；用 60 帧拍、按 24 帧放，就是 2.5 倍慢动作。" = "24 fps means 24 pictures every second; 60 fps means 60. More frames make motion smoother. Shoot at 60 and play back at 24 and you get 2.5× slow motion.";
"每一帧要有一点拖影" = "Each frame needs a little blur";
"快门太快，每帧都清清楚楚，连起来反而一跳一跳。常用做法是快门约等于 1/(2×帧率)：24 帧用 1/50，30 帧用 1/60（叫 180° 快门）。白天太亮时，要加 ND 滤镜减光，而不是提高快门。" = "With a very fast shutter every frame is crisp, and played together the motion looks jerky. The usual rule is a shutter of about 1/(2 × frame rate): 1/50 at 24 fps, 1/60 at 30 fps (the “180° shutter”). When daylight is too bright, cut the light with an ND filter instead of raising the shutter speed.";
"用 25 帧拍视频，按这个原则快门该设多少？" = "Shooting video at 25 fps, what shutter speed does this rule give?";
"1/1000 秒" = "1/1000 s";
"1/25 秒" = "1/25 s";
"1/50 秒" = "1/50 s";
"1/(2×25) = 1/50 秒，动作自然。1/1000 太快，画面会有卡顿感。" = "1/(2 × 25) = 1/50 s, for natural motion. 1/1000 is too fast and makes motion look choppy.";
"Log 素材与 LUT" = "Log Footage and LUTs";
"D-Log 拍出来为什么灰蒙蒙的？" = "Why does D-Log footage look so gray and flat?";
"Log 把更多亮度装进同一个文件" = "Log fits more brightness into the same file";
"普通模式（Rec.709）亮到一定程度就变成纯白。Log 用一条平缓的曲线，把很暗到很亮都记下来，代价是画面看起来又灰又淡。拖动「场景亮度」比较两条线。" = "In normal mode (Rec.709), anything past a certain brightness turns pure white. Log uses a gentle curve to record everything from very dark to very bright, at the cost of a gray, washed-out look. Drag “Scene brightness” to compare the two lines.";
"LUT 把它还原成正常画面" = "A LUT turns it back into a normal picture";
"转换 LUT 是一张对照表：在颜色空间里放一张网，把网上每个点搬到新的位置。拖动强度，看这张网被拉开，照片的颜色和直方图一起铺开。注意：这里用你的照片模拟 Log 的样子。" = "A conversion LUT is a lookup table: it puts a grid into color space and moves every point on the grid to a new position. Drag the strength and watch the grid stretch open, with the photo's colors and histogram spreading out together. Note: this simulates the Log look using your photo.";
"拿到 D-Log 素材，第一步做什么？" = "You've got D-Log footage. What's the first step?";
"先套用这台相机对应的转换 LUT" = "Apply this camera's conversion LUT first";
"直接拉高饱和度和对比度" = "Just raise saturation and contrast";
"降低曝光" = "Lower the exposure";
"先用厂商的转换 LUT 回到正常画面，再在上面调色；直接拉滑块很难还原准确的颜色。" = "Use the maker's conversion LUT to get back to a normal image, then adjust on top of it. Pushing sliders alone rarely gets the colors right.";

